00:08:04.350 --> 00:08:07.386
to the 15th vote to get to that gavel.

00:08:07.587 --> 00:08:09.589
What are the next two years look like

00:08:09.589 --> 00:08:11.457
if you have these members there on

00:08:11.457 --> 00:08:12.158
House Oversight

00:08:13.893 --> 00:08:14.727
Dysfunction,

00:08:14.727 --> 00:08:16.028
dysfunction, dysfunction,

00:08:16.028 --> 00:08:16.896
that is what the next

00:08:16.896 --> 00:08:18.030
two years look like.

00:08:18.030 --> 00:08:18.931
And it saddens me

00:08:18.931 --> 00:08:19.966
as somebody who has worked

00:08:19.966 --> 00:08:20.867
in the halls of Congress

00:08:20.867 --> 00:08:21.767
and any of those

00:08:21.767 --> 00:08:23.169
any of us who worked in the halls

00:08:23.169 --> 00:08:24.871
know we know that

00:08:24.871 --> 00:08:26.973
not only are these members, these people

00:08:26.973 --> 00:08:29.041
we elect as our representatives,

00:08:29.041 --> 00:08:30.877
people who should be committed

00:08:30.877 --> 00:08:32.345
to intellectual debate,

00:08:32.345 --> 00:08:34.347
rigorous intellectual debate,

00:08:34.347 --> 00:08:35.214
but they should also,

00:08:35.214 --> 00:08:37.316
at the very least, have stable minds.

00:08:37.550 --> 00:08:38.885
And what I think we've seen

00:08:38.885 --> 00:08:39.485
with the Crazy

00:08:39.485 --> 00:08:40.052
Clown Car

00:08:40.052 --> 00:08:42.555
Caucus of Kosar and Gates and Boebert

00:08:42.722 --> 00:08:45.758
we've seen this lack of desire to govern.

00:08:46.359 --> 00:08:48.327
We've seen this want to blow it all up.

00:08:48.327 --> 00:08:49.428
And this is a problem

00:08:49.428 --> 00:08:50.463
in our moment right now

00:08:50.463 --> 00:08:51.464
where we have this

00:08:51.464 --> 00:08:52.365
these attitudes

00:08:52.365 --> 00:08:54.300
that are all or nothing attitudes.

00:08:54.300 --> 00:08:55.801
They are creating the problem

00:08:55.801 --> 00:08:57.803
that messes with everyday governing.

00:08:57.870 --> 00:08:59.605
So it's what's happening in our politics

00:08:59.605 --> 00:09:01.574
doesn't just happen over there.

00:09:01.574 --> 00:09:03.342
It affects what happens on the Hill

00:09:03.342 --> 00:09:05.011
because they bring these attitudes

00:09:05.011 --> 00:09:05.678
and then they

00:09:05.678 --> 00:09:06.812
they at every moment

00:09:06.812 --> 00:09:08.948
want to create barriers to progress,

00:09:09.115 --> 00:09:10.149
to things actually

00:09:10.149 --> 00:09:11.551
getting done for the American people.

00:09:11.551 --> 00:09:12.251
And conservatives

00:09:12.251 --> 00:09:13.619
have real opportunities.

00:09:13.619 --> 00:09:14.887
When we talk about economy,

00:09:14.887 --> 00:09:16.556
immigration, energy.

00:09:16.556 --> 00:09:17.356
These are places

00:09:17.356 --> 00:09:19.492
that Republicans can lead this year.

00:09:19.625 --> 00:09:20.760
They can legislate.

00:09:20.760 --> 00:09:22.028
They can choose to govern.

00:09:22.028 --> 00:09:23.396
But again, these people

00:09:23.396 --> 00:09:25.364
who are characterizing our politics,

00:09:25.364 --> 00:09:26.666
they've made it so hard

00:09:26.666 --> 00:09:28.167
because they've made it so difficult

00:09:28.167 --> 00:09:29.135
for Kevin McCarthy

00:09:29.135 --> 00:09:31.337
to afford to lose even one vote

00:09:31.337 --> 00:09:32.605
like I mentioned earlier.

00:09:32.605 --> 00:09:34.440
And that is it's a very simple reason

00:09:34.440 --> 00:09:35.942
for why we will see the dysfunction in

00:09:35.942 --> 00:09:36.842
the next two years.

